# PART 5: ERRORS ENCOUNTERED AND CORRECTED COMMANDS

## Error 1: Port 8080 Already in Use

### Incorrect command attempted

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8080:80 nginx
```

### Error

```text
ports are not available:
bind: Only one usage of each socket address is normally permitted
```

### Reason

Port `8080` was already being used by another application, possibly Jenkins.

### Correct command

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

Open:

```text
http://localhost:8082
```

## Error 2: Container Name Already in Use

### Command attempted

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

### Error

```text
Conflict. The container name "/nginxdemo" is already in use
```

### Reason

The previous failed attempt had already created a container with the same name.

### Solution

Check all containers:

```bash
docker ps -a
```

Remove the old container:

```bash
docker rm nginxdemo
```

Run again:

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

Alternative one-command solution:

```bash
docker rm -f nginxdemo
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

## Error 3: Docker Cannot Resolve Docker Hub DNS

### Command attempted

```bash
docker run -d --name nagiosdemo -p 8888:80 jasonrivers/nagios:latest
```

### Error

```text
failed to resolve reference
lookup registry-1.docker.io: no such host
```

### Reason

Docker could not resolve the Docker Hub hostname. This is a DNS or network connectivity issue.

### Step 1: Check Internet

```bash
ping google.com
```

### Step 2: Check Docker Hub DNS

```bash
nslookup registry-1.docker.io
```

### Step 3: Restart Docker Desktop

Open Docker Desktop → Troubleshoot → Restart Docker Desktop.

If DNS still fails, check your Windows network DNS settings. On a network where public DNS is permitted, you can try:

```text
Preferred DNS: 8.8.8.8
Alternate DNS: 8.8.4.4
```

### Step 4: Test Docker Hub Connection

```bash
docker pull hello-world
```

### Step 5: Pull Nagios Again

```bash
docker pull jasonrivers/nagios:latest
```

### Step 6: Run Nagios

```bash
docker run -d --name nagiosdemo -p 8888:80 jasonrivers/nagios:latest
```

